    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on maximizing speed and plate appearances against mid-tier rotations. **Brice Turang** earns our top score of 63.99, serving as the cornerstone of the daily strategy. His elevated mark is driven by his elite sprint speed against Roki Sasaki; Sasaki\u2019s deliberate delivery provides a high-probability environment for **Turang** to swipe a base, and his projected role in the #2 hole maximizes his exposure to potential RBI opportunities. While **Travis Bazzana** (53.06) and **Seiya Suzuki** (51.86) offer solid mid-range utility, the decision to slot **Turang** into the UTIL spot over other bench options remains our most significant efficiency play.\n\nThe decision to start **Josh Naylor** (55.47) despite a challenging matchup against Fried requires careful monitoring. While Fried\u2019s 3.80 xERA presents a hurdle, **Naylor**\u2019s strong recent form and the slight boost from batting fifth in the order keep him well above our floor. Conversely, **Jose Caballero** (42.15) occupies the most marginal spot in today's lineup. His score is suppressed by a tough matchup against Logan Gilbert and a lower spot in the order, but his status as a primary speed engine for our squad necessitates his inclusion. With **James Wood** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** currently sidelined on the IL, and **Corbin Carroll** and **Tyler Soderstrom** off the schedule today, our depth is being tested. **Seiya Suzuki**\u2019s projection remains contingent on his confirmation in the #2 spot; should he drop down the order, his efficiency score will likely dip, putting him in a near-toss-up category with depth pieces like **Zach McKinstry** or **Henry Bolte**. Regardless of the daily variance, we are prioritizing players capable of exploiting aggressive baserunning opportunities to keep our SB category competitive.",
